+# --- DNK-MRH-HEADER ---
+# mrh_id: "plugins/google-vertex-media/README.md"
+# purpose: "Comprehensive architecture, configuration, and reverse-engineering guide for Google Cloud Vertex Media."
+# canonical_source: true
+# alters_files: []
+# triggers_tasks: []
+# status: "Active"
+# version: "1.0.0"
+# updated_at: "2026-11-08"
+# --- END DNK-MRH-HEADER ---
+
+# Google Cloud Vertex AI Media Plugin (Imagen 3/4 & Veo 3.1)
+
+A unified, self-contained media generation plugin for Hermes Agent and external agent harnesses (LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, OpenAI/LiteLLM, Anthropic).
+
+## 🌟 Key Highlights
+
+1. **Dual Media Engine**:
+   - **Google Imagen 3 / Imagen 4**: High-resolution image generation, studio aesthetics, photorealism, and typography.
+   - **Google Veo 3.1**: Cinematic video generation (Text-to-Video and Image-to-Video) with native synchronized audio generation and realistic physics.
+2. **First-Class Hermes Agent Integration**:
+   - Registers as standard `image_gen` provider (`image_gen.provider: vertex`).
+   - Registers as standard `video_gen` provider (`video_gen.provider: vertex`).
+   - Provides direct standalone tools `google_imagen` and `google_veo` (usable regardless of default provider).
+   - Provides CLI commands `hermes vertex-media {image|video|status|export|serve|install-user}`.
+3. **Decoupled Architecture & Reverse-Engineering Ready**:
+   - Clean, zero-dependency client (`client.py`) that can be used completely outside Hermes Agent.
+   - Built-in schema exporters: OpenAI Function Calling, Anthropic Claude Tools, LangChain StructuredTools, and CrewAI Tools.
+   - Built-in HTTP REST bridge (`hermes vertex-media serve`) providing OpenAI-compatible endpoints (`/v1/images/generations`, `/v1/videos/generations`, `/v1/tools/call`).
+4. **Update-Proof Persistence**:
+   - Supports user-profile deployment in `~/.hermes/plugins/google-vertex-media/`.
+   - Running `hermes vertex-media install-user` installs the plugin outside the git repository, ensuring subsequent git pulls or `hermes update` runs never overwrite your plugin.
+
+---
+
+## 🔑 Authentication & Configuration
+
+The plugin automatically resolves Google Cloud credentials in the following order:
+
+1. **Hermes Native Adapter**: Reads `vertex.project_id`, `vertex.region`, `vertex.credentials_path` from `~/.hermes/config.yaml`.
+2. **Environment Variables**:
+   - `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`: Path to Service Account JSON.
+   - `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` or `GCP_PROJECT`: Project ID.
+   - `VERTEX_REGION`: Target region (default: `us-central1`).
+   - `VERTEX_BEARER_TOKEN`: Pre-generated OAuth2 access token.
+3. **Google ADC (Application Default Credentials)**: Auto-detected via `google.auth.default()`.
+4. **gcloud CLI Fallback**: Uses `gcloud auth print-access-token` if installed.
+
+### Quick Verification
+```bash
+hermes vertex-media status
+```
+
+---
+
+## ⚙️ Hermes Agent Configuration
+
+To use Vertex AI as your default provider for `image_generate` and `video_generate`, add the following to `~/.hermes/config.yaml`:
+
+```yaml
+image_gen:
+  provider: vertex
+
+video_gen:
+  provider: vertex
+
+vertex:
+  project_id: "your-gcp-project-id"
+  region: "us-central1"
+```
+
+---
+
+## 🛠️ Direct Tools
+
+### 1. `google_imagen`
+```json
+{
+  "prompt": "Cinematic portrait of a cybersecurity architect in a neon server room, 35mm lens, photorealistic",
+  "model": "imagen-3.0-generate-002",
+  "aspect_ratio": "16:9",
+  "number_of_images": 1
+}
+```
+
+### 2. `google_veo`
+```json
+{
+  "prompt": "Drone shot flying over snow-covered pine forests at sunset, cinematic lighting, 4k",
+  "model": "veo-3.1-generate-001",
+  "aspect_ratio": "16:9",
+  "resolution": "720p",
+  "duration": 6,
+  "audio": true
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## 💻 CLI Commands
+
+```bash
+# Generate image
+hermes vertex-media image "Futuristic electric sports car in Kyiv" --aspect-ratio 16:9
+
+# Generate video with Veo 3.1
+hermes vertex-media video "Ocean waves crashing against volcanic rocks" --duration 6
+
+# Export tools for other harnesses
+hermes vertex-media export --format openai
+hermes vertex-media export --format anthropic
+
+# Run local HTTP bridge server
+hermes vertex-media serve --port 8190
+
+# Install to ~/.hermes/plugins/ (survives updates)
+hermes vertex-media install-user
+```
+
+---
+
+## 🔄 Reverse-Engineering for External Agent Harnesses
+
+### Using in LangChain / LangGraph
+```python
+from plugins.google_vertex_media.harness import to_langchain_tools
+
+tools = to_langchain_tools()
+# Bind directly to your LangChain agent / model
+agent_executor = create_react_agent(model, tools)
+```
+
+### Using with OpenAI SDK / LiteLLM
+```python
+import openai
+from plugins.google_vertex_media.harness import dispatch_tool, to_openai_tools
+
+client = openai.OpenAI()
+tools = to_openai_tools()
+
+response = client.chat.completions.create(
+    model="gpt-4o",
+    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "Generate a video of a sunrise over the mountains"}],
+    tools=tools,
+)
+
+tool_call = response.choices[0].message.tool_calls[0]
+result = dispatch_tool(tool_call.function.name, tool_call.function.arguments)
+print(result)
+```
+
+### Using with Anthropic Claude API
+```python
+import anthropic
+from plugins.google_vertex_media.harness import dispatch_tool, to_anthropic_tools
+
+client = anthropic.Anthropic()
+tools = to_anthropic_tools()
+
+response = client.messages.create(
+    model="claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219",
+    max_tokens=1024,
+    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "Draw an abstract logo for DNK OS"}],
+    tools=tools,
+)
+```
+
+### Using via Standalone REST API (cURL / Any Language)
+Start the bridge:
+```bash
+hermes vertex-media serve --port 8190
+```
+
+Call from cURL:
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8190/v1/images/generations \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"prompt": "Ukrainian cybernetic kozak in high-tech armor", "size": "1792x1024"}'
+```
